WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.200
Grab your spandex and listen up, because we
have an all-new season of "American Horror Story"

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.700
and Think Story is here to take
a deep dive into each episode.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.020
I'm not gonna waste any of
your time, so let's get right into it.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.180
We're in 1970, baby, at
beautiful Camp Redwood,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.440
which, if you've seen the
trailer, doesn't turn out so well.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.240
We're introduced to these
two, who we saw in the trailer,

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.800
and this dude and
his lambskin condoms,

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.840
because you never know when
a girl will be allergic to latex.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.520
We hear the clanging of Mr. Jingles' keys,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.740
who we've seen from the trailer is
supposedly the main bad guy this season.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.940
Yes, we can confirm that we're in the middle of
camp season and these teens are camp counselors.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.100
Notice also the grain in the film here,
which isn't shown in the 1984 scenes,

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.400
so if you ever see this grain,
we're likely dealing with a flashback

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.120
that mimics the style and
feel of an old 80's slasher.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:00.660
We see this later on with the flashback
of Mr. Jingles working at Camp Redwood.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:06.160
And as soon as this girl takes her top off, these two
are dead, which is officially the worst cockblock ever.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.880
Here we get our first glimpse of the hand of Mr. Jingles and the sound of his keys, which we see here briefly.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.420
And here's a shot of me watching
the final season of Game of Thrones.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.760
Now, the creators make an effort to show
Jingles cutting off this camper's ear.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.820
Serial killers have been known
to take tokens of their victims,

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.620
so expect these ears to come
into play later on in the season.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:31.160
We also see the extent of the massacre
and that Jingles walks with a limp.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.480
Now this makes sense since

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.280
many of the early slasher villains like Jason
Voorhees or Michael Myers walked very slowly,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.480
so making Jingles unable to run is
keeping in line with that tradition.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.640
But what is most revealing about this scene is
the exclusion of Leslie Grossman's character,

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:52.660
who we saw in the trailer as being in
that very cabin the night of the massacre.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.580
We'll meet her a bit later on as the
owner of the camp, Margaret Booth.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:04.160
Now, in my trailer video, I theorized that her character
is my number 1 pick of being the real or surprise killer.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.540
And just this morning, I got a message from Twitter
user Cael Harden, who expanded on this idea that

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:15.780
Jingles is actually coming back to exact revenge
on Margaret and possibly to save the other campers.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.480
The theory goes that he was framed for the
massacre and that Margaret was the real killer.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.040
And so far, it's making a lot of sense.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.840
She's a religious nutjob who decides to
reopen the camp where she almost died.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.720
Her affinity to remain pure and
clean would also give her motive

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.840
to kill the philandering teens
at the beginning of the episode,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:40.520
which coincides with the plots of many 80's
horror where a killer goes after horny teens.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:46.360
Now we have our look at the new intro titles, which
can also give some interesting clues about the season.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:51.020
Notice the 4:3 aspect ratio, which
is similar to those of VHS movies,

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.980
and the 1980's music
video style and retro graphics.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.740
We also get a few shots of the camp,

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:00.640
but what I think is most revealing
in this is the inclusion of the ear.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:04.560
But also of this ear with
sound waves going into it.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.920
We've already seen that Jingles likes to cut off
ears, so pay attention to this in episodes to come.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:13.440
Speaking of Jingles, we
also get this quick shot of keys.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:19.900
And the 80's were huge with montages, so we get a quick 80's dance montage with our favorite son of Satan,

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.660
who is looking more like
the son of Richard Simmons.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:32.140
Here we get introduced to our main cast:
Xavier, Montana, Ray, Chet and Brooke.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.460
But it looks like both Brooke
and Chet are going to hit it off.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:39.400
Montana remarks on Brooke
ogling Chet's, ahem, mound.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.480
As I suspected in my trailer video,
she might be into girls herself,

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.820
talking about how
great Brooke's butt is,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.560
but considering she used to
date Xavier, it's likely she's bi.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.760
Brooke, however,
isn't here to hook up.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:56.180
It looks like her character will be
that of the stereotypical slasher virgin,

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.660
a trope which I'm sure Ryan
 Murphy will hopefully subvert.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.980
In the lobby, Xavier
remarks about the Night Stalker,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.280
a serial killer on the loose who
apparently stabbed someone 40 times,

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.480
almost decapitating his victim.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.900
Chet introduces himself to
Brooke and she creams her pants.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:19.660
We learn that Montana "rear-ended Xavier while in traffic", which is a very graphic double entendre.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:24.680
Xavier is a method actor who trained
under the real acting guru Stella Adler.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:27.700
And Ray met Chet at a party
where Justine Bateman was,

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:32.560
who was an actual actress known for
the 1984 show "Tales from the Darkside".

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.480
Summer is gonna be crazy
in L.A. due to the Olympics,

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:40.800
and Xavier suggests they all get a summer job
as counselors a few hours away from the city,

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.740
while Montana writes her number on
Brooke's arm in case she's interested.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:48.500
While at home, Brooke removes her
earring, yet another reference to ears,

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.220
when she is later
attacked by the Night Stalker.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.420
He somehow knows she has jewelry and
although his attempt at killing her is thwarted,

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.000
he says, "I will find you.
Satan will show me the way".

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:04.840
Considering how much last season focused on Satan,
I wouldn't be surprised if there's some crossover here.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.800
Also, considering how we know L.A. has a satanist cult that was seen last season, who knows if they'll show up.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:15.340
Rather than stay at home with the Night Stalker
still on the loose and knowing where she lives,

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.540
Brooke ventures off with the gang
and Montana gets a little close.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.080
We learn that Chet was about to be an
Olympian when he was disqualified for drug use.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.880
And for you young kids
out there, that's a polaroid.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Fuck, I'm old.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:33.240
At a roadside gas station, we meet this lovely
character, Ed, according to his name tag.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.800
And yes, he is Patrick Swayze's brother.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:39.520
Notice his ring of keys here, which
Mr. Jingles will later take from him.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.920
Xavier checks his voicemail on the
pay phone with what appears to be

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.120
a jealous ex lover
saying he's going to find him.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.560
Could Xavier's ex be the Night
Stalker, which leads him to Brooke?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.320
While seemingly lost on the
way, Xavier runs over this guy.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.220
But what's mysterious is the fact
he says he can't remember his name.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:02.500
Now, we don't know if this is the result
of him getting hit or if it happened prior,

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:08.540
since, as Xavier notes, he already had dried blood
and cuts that happened to him before the accident.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:13.200
The hiker also says a menacing
line, "You gotta believe me, I tried."

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.580
So expect this to be expanded on later.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.560
The counselors arrive at Camp
Redwood where we meet Margaret

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.520
and we're told that the kids are
supposed to arrive in the morning.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:25.100
But first things first, they got
to get this hiker to the infirmary.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.160
There, they meet Rita, who tells them
she used to work at Hawthorne Hospital.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:33.900
Now might just be coincidence, but the Hawthorne School for Exceptional Young Men was where

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:38.420
Michael Langdon was trained and where
most of the events of Apocalypse take place.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:43.360
They lie to Rita, saying they found the hiker on
the side of the road when they actually hit him.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:45.520
Margaret then shows
them to their quarters.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:49.400
We get a few shots of the lake
and an introduction to Chef Bertie,

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.920
who was around when
Margaret was just a camper.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.500
This is our first indication that Margaret was
indeed a camper before she reopened the camp

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.160
after "One bad apple ruined it",

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.700
a reference to Mr. Jingles and the massacre.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.540
Margaret tells them that the girls shower
in the a.m. and the boys in the p.m.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:09.320
And we've already seen in the trailer
someone peeping at one of the male's showering,

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:16.240
who I surmise, due to eye color, as being either Xavier or Matthew Morrison's character, who we'll meet in a bit.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:20.080
After Margaret shows them to their
cabins, we learn that she's a religious zealot

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.080
who fights "the Lord's fight against filth".

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.620
She stood alongside Charles Keating, who
was a real-life anti-pornography advocate

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:30.320
famous for his crusade against Larry Flynt .

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:35.360
And we learn her husband died, leaving her with
a fortune, which she used to reopen the camp

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.460
and make it a godly
place for children to escape.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:42.160
Very convenient for her husband to
die and leave her with all this money.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:46.660
Around the campfire, Rita tells the
counselors about the Camp Redwood massacre,

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.520
which happened 14 years ago.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:54.260
And we get a little bit of an origin story
for Mr. Jingles aka Benjamin Richter.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:58.120
Apparently, he was a Vietnam veteran
who collected the ears of his kills

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.840
and became somewhat of
a groundskeeper at Redwood

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.680
when one day he snapped,
murdering all the female counselors.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:09.620
There was one survivor, however, Margaret,
who says through the power of Christ

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:15.340
was able to leave her body while she was
having her ear sawed off as to not make a sound.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.600
She hopes that by
reopening Camp Redwood,

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:21.680
she can turn the dark memories she
had into something bright and happy.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:25.220
The hiker awakens in the middle of the
night and checks himself in the mirror

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.700
to find out that he
has also lost his ear.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.400
Now, this has happened
before Jingles' arrival,

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.660
so there's obviously someone
else perpetrating these acts.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.780
Brooke decides to check
on the hiker, or so she says.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:40.580
I can't help but feel she's in that
infirmary for a different reason.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.640
She's startled by the hiker, who tells
her that the phone lines are down,

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:46.100
because it wouldn't be an
80's slasher if they weren't.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.820
And when she tries to comfort him, he seems
confused that Camp Redwood has reopened.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.160
Back at the cabin, we're introduced to
everyone's favorite Glee teacher, Matthew Morrison.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:01.300
He plays a character named Trevor, who was cut
from a Jane Fonda video for being too distracting.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.500
"That thing was flopping around
like a baby elephant's trunk."

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.000
It's skinny-dipping time, and Trevor and
Montana are already breaking Margaret's rules.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:13.200
They're interrupted by an impending
storm and a pair of spooky headlights.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:17.240
Now, we haven't seen Jingles arrive
yet, he arrives later when it's raining.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:22.060
So my guess is that this is someone
else, likely Margaret keeping tabs on them.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:28.100
We're then introduced to Dr. Hopple in what appears
to be a scene straight out of 1978's "Halloween"

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.960
with a patient, Mr. Jingles, having escaped.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:36.260
3 hours earlier, he killed an orderly and
escaped, taking his glasses and keys with him.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:41.760
We learned earlier that Ray is also an orderly, so
it will be interesting if there is a connection here.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:46.840
Hopple inspects the cell to find a newspaper
clipping about the reopening of Camp Redwood

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.040
with Margaret's picture circled in blood.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:53.060
Jingles is going back to Redwood
to put an end to its only survivor.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:56.260
Or perhaps to seek
revenge, if the theory is correct.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.220
Back at the gas station, Ed works on a car,
and take a look at these delicious hot dogs.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:05.500
And you know, if you're underneath a car in
a horror show, this isn't gonna turn out well.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.900
Mr. Jingles completely
destroys him and takes his keys.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:14.880
Also note that Jingles has killed 2 people so far
and hasn't taken either of their ears as tokens.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:20.160
Chet goes full roid rage after seeing the opening
of the Olympics and is pissed he isn't there.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:23.680
He throws a crushed beer can
at Ray, who gets a massive cut,

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:27.200
and Rita refuses to help
because she's the worst nurse ever.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:30.640
- "Nurse, a little help?"
- "I clocked out already. I'm here for the kids."

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.760
Brooke looks after Ray and
they share a little moment here.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.060
So if we go by the horror trope
that the virgin character will survive,

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:40.440
it usually means her love
interest is one of the first to go.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:41.860
So watch out, Ray.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.720
Brooke says she'll look for some iodine and
bandages, when she notices the hiker hanging out

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:51.060
with the sound and image of what
appears to be Mr. Jingles watching her.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:56.220
We don't see the perpetrator's face here, which
leads me to believe we're dealing with the second killer,

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.240
someone who is
motivated to keep the hiker quiet.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.120
But this character has a
limp and you can hear the keys,

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:06.240
so it's either one of three things:
Margaret trying to keep in character,

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.040
Jingles trying to save
Brooke from the real killer,

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:12.940
or I'm just thinking way too hard on this
and it's simply Jingles trying to kill her.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:17.400
As Brooke runs, I love how it's juxtaposed
with the lighting of the Olympic torch.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:22.340
She tells the other counselors what she saw
and when they go to investigate, they find nothing.

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:24.800
Also, Montana has
the worst shield ever.

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.360
And look who's there to usher
them back to their cabins?

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:31.740
Margaret, who just so happens to be
in a similar raincoat to Mr. Jingles.

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:34.660
Brooke seems to be the only
one noticing this phone ringing

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.960
and wakes up Montana, who
we find sleeps with a switchblade.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:39.920
You know that switchblade
is gonna come back.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:44.140
Brooke ends up answering the phone
when we hear the clang of Mr. Jingles' keys

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.660
and see the arrival of the Night Stalker.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:50.080
This is accompanied by Brooke
asking the person on the phone who it is

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:53.960
and if you listen carefully, you
can hear the response "Satan".

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:58.060
We know the Night Stalker is a
follower of Satan, so this makes sense.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:00.380
That's it for my
episode 1 breakdown, guys.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:02.560
I am super pumped about this season.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:06.460
I think it was a fantastic first
episode, set up a lot of stuff,

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.360
but I want to hear what you thought
about it in the thoughts below.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:12.360
Make sure to give the video a like
and subscribe with the bell on,

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:15.220
as I plan to do
breakdowns of every episode.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:19.760
You can also follow me and send me
theories to my Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.560
Until next time remember,

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.680
Daddy loves you very much.

